the head of unlv breaks his silence  after a student died following a  fraternity boxing match it's a story our  i-team first broke and now the i-team  has the president's first interview  president keith whitfield sent an email  to the university community but he  hasn't answered questions until now  vanessa murphy has the story from campus  this is the first time unlv president  keith whitfield agreed to answer  questions about the fraternity boxing  match which ended with one student's  death this student was a part of our  family and we're actually you know  it's it's a little emotional for me to  even be thinking and talking about it  president whitfield says he talked with  nathan valencia's father to express  condolences valencia seen here in the  red headgear participated in this  fraternity boxing match on november 19th  he collapsed after the fight and died  four days later from head injuries  valencia's family points to a lack of  safety precautions like no paramedics or  professional medical help on standby and  a referee who they say was unlicensed  the i-team obtained this video where he  appears to be drinking alcohol the  family points out the event is a unlv  tradition and they say the university  and kappa sigma fraternity which held  the event are to blame what oversight  did the university have and what leaders  at the university did know this was  going to happen  that's one of the questions that we're  asking in this fact-finding uh  let's not call an investigation it's a  review of our procedures that we want to  go through  not only for this group but for all  programs on our campus  you mentioned a review is underway  but at this point as the leader of this  university who do you think should be  held accountable  well you know it's premature to say  exactly who we  want to  to start pointing fingers on about  accountability we're going to do a very  very thorough process and we're going to  make sure that we identify all the parts  and pieces of how this played out  on wednesday unlv announced the kappa  sigma fraternity is suspended the  valencia's family attorney tells me this  is a step in the right direction  reporting in las vegas vanessa murphy  live local now
 

